  "limitations": [
    "Two short measured phases per target, short proxy warmup, one JVM each and no confidence intervals or independent forks.",
    "Generator, fixture, both proxies and any other environment activity compete for the same cgroup resources.",
    "The Netty app includes command/Resilience4j overhead; the Jetty demo has no corresponding command layer. This compares complete configured stacks.",
    "Connection totals are matched nominally; Netty partitions pools/queues per event loop and Jetty uses a destination-wide pool/queue.",
    "Netty response read-ahead buffer is four chunks; Jetty uses its one-write demand-driven path. These are different flow-control implementations.",
    "Cleartext loopback HTTP/1.1, streaming identity payload only; no TLS, Security, multipart, rewrite, slow-client or overload throughput measurement.",
    "CPU snapshots include the JMeter launch/finish window. RSS/HWM/thread snapshots are not allocator accounting or a bound on direct memory.",
    "Direct-origin CPU is the Python fixture/orchestrator process, not a Java proxy. Generator CPU includes runner/hash validation activity."
  ],
